 ## Overview
-Score-based Densification is a constructive densification strategy for 3D Gaussian Splatting that controls model size by adding new primitives only to those that maximize reconstruction quality, adhering to a strict, user-defined budget without requiring pruning or culling during training [S1]. Unlike standard 3D Gaussian Splatting which relies on opacity-based pruning to manage redundancy, this method ensures a predictable growth curve and fixed final model size, making it suitable for hardware-constrained environments [S1].
+Score-based Densification is a constructive densification strategy for 3D Gaussian Splatting that controls model size by adding new Gaussians only to those primitives that maximize a specific quality score, adhering to a pre-defined user budget [S1]. Unlike standard 3D Gaussian Splatting which relies on aggressive pruning and splitting without strict size caps, this method ensures the final model size is predictable and bounded, avoiding the optimization instability caused by large-scale culling [S1]. It is designed for scenarios where hardware memory or storage constraints require a fixed-capacity output [S1].
 
 ## How it works
-The method replaces the heuristic-based splitting of standard 3D Gaussian Splatting with a guided, score-driven process that selects Gaussians for densification based on their contribution to the loss [S1].
